Need to test && and ||  Actually tested already; seems to work
Prefix operators (Clod, 2026-10-26): prevOp marks "the previous entry was an operator, or there was none"; an operator
arriving then is a PENDING PREFIX (pre) that wraps the next operand (negate / deref), so it never overwrites the pending
binary op. qc - - qa, - qa + qb, qa - - qb + qc, * qa + qb, righty = - qa + qb now build right. Running a unary through
testOP needs branch testop-unary-slot (testOP read slot 3; the unary operand is in slot 2) -- until it is bought,
testOP on a chain with a prefix exits 139. The old `or *target.instructTypE != 0; kind = 3;` rule is gone with kind 3.
Tiers (Clod, SEQ 434, 2026-10-27): arithmetic folds at once; compare (compareTier), logic (shortCircuit) and assign
(assignTier) each wait in their own pending slot (cmpP, logP, asgP). A looser operator first closes every tighter slot
into the target, an equal one closes its own (so a tier reads left to right, as kant does: qc > qa || qa > qc && qb > qc
is 0), and assign never closes assign. The end closes the slots tightest first. qa > qb + qc, righty = 0 || qb > qc and
qa > qc && qb > qc || qc > qa now build as kant reads them (testerChainT TC-3c, TC-4b, TC-11, TC-12). Still open: a
third assign is untested (a second nests through asgO, measured); + on a null target now refuses by name (op-own-write).
